  "content": {
    "id": "p38-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "If one hundred coins are tossed onto the floor, then the most likely outcome is that fifty of them land heads and fifty land tails. However, what is the probability of this actually happening? Use a calculator to find an answer accurate to two decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$0.08$",
      "worked": "Let $X$ count heads. For independent fair coins, $X$ has binomial distribution with $n=100$ and $p=\\frac12$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(X=50)&=\\binom{100}{50}\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{50}\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{50}\\\\\\Pr(X=50)&=\\frac{\\binom{100}{50}}{2^{100}}\\\\\\Pr(X=50)&\\approx0.08\\quad\\text{(2 decimal places).}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 24
  },
